  "discussion": "A moderate, long-period northwest swell will peak today, producing surf around seasonal average along north and exposed west-facing shores. This swell will begin to decline late today and fade by Thursday. A small, short-period north-northeast swell will maintain through much of the week, and may even become moderate for some time during the latter half of the week with the arrival of reinforcing energy from the northeast. A moderate, long-period northwest swell is forecast to arrive this weekend, with potential to reach advisory levels by Sunday. Overlapping south-southwest swells will keep surf along south-facing shores near seasonal average today. A slightly larger south swell arriving tonight pushes surf above seasonal average for Wednesday. Additional south energy may prolong near to above average surf for south-facing shores on Thursday and Friday as well. Surf along most east-facing shores will be small through the first half of the week, but areas exposed to wrapping northerly swells will experience periods of moderate surf. East-facing shores should also see a bump in surf with the northeast swell during the latter half of this week.",
